laws bc_sat_areab_only sub_sat_emission_ns diode_wl_mult_once diode_sidewall_own_f1 diode_xom_absent_1e14 vdmos_kp_absent_20 vdmos_tcvth_raises vdmos_clamp_by_fc mos_small_signal_exact mos6_small_signal_exact bjt_irb_small_signal_exact vdmos_mult_charges_copies diode_isr_reverse_present diode_isr_small_signal_exact diode_tt_factor_clamped trig_exact exp_exact log_zero_error div_exact asin_edge_fails default_temp_27 default_tnom_27 bsim4v45_small_signal_exact
# Oracle: runs (R99b, F61; runrules-2 step3-runrules 30680875, ace6399e,
# tests/passes_run/decks/f33_frac_vacask_*): VACASK truncates a non-integer `points` toward zero,
# silently, a literal and an expression alike (dec 2.4, 2.5, 2.6 run 2 per decade; lin 1.5 runs as
# 1 interval, 2.5 as 2; dec 5.0/2 runs 2 per decade). A literal count is read as its truncation (a
# lin count of intervals then plus one); an expression not of Int type is wrapped in `to_int`
# (VACASK's `int`, truncation toward zero); an Int expression stands as it is.
# codes:
file "b_points_frac.sim" deck
  title "non-integer sweep counts"
  analysis ac name=a1 (dec start=1k stop=100k points=2i)
  analysis ac name=a2 (dec start=1k stop=100k points=2i)
  analysis ac name=a3 (lin start=1k stop=2k points=2i)
  analysis ac name=a4 (lin start=1k stop=2k points=3i)
  analysis ac name=a5 (dec start=1k stop=100k points=(to_int(5.0 /: 2i)))
  analysis ac name=a6 (lin start=1k stop=2k points=(to_int(5.0 /: 2i) + 1i))
  analysis ac name=a7 (dec start=1k stop=100k points=(2i * 2i))
